=begin pod

=TITLE App::FontSample TODO

=SUBTITLE Planned improvements after the current release

=head1 PURPOSE

This file contains planned work for C<App::FontSample>. These items are not
current capabilities and therefore are intentionally kept out of the user
documentation in C<README.rakudoc>.

=head1 LAYOUTS

=item Add a dedicated waterfall-only renderer instead of using the specimen
renderer for C<waterfall>.

=item Continue improving the comparison and collection layouts for larger
font sets and more varied sample text.

=item Consider additional layouts for language samples and font metrics.

=head1 CHARACTER AND GLYPH DISPLAY

=item Add optional character-cell borders.

=item Add optional baseline and cap-height guides.

=item Add small left and right edge tick marks for visual font-metric
inspection.

=item Extend C<characters> input with convenient Unicode range notation such
as C<0020..007E>.

=item Investigate named Unicode block selection.

=item Improve handling and presentation of characters not present in the
selected font.

=head1 LANGUAGE SAMPLES

=item Expand the built-in language sample and pangram registry.

=item Document which sample languages are covered by commonly used font
families.

=item Continue making it easy for applications to supply additional language
samples without modifying C<App::FontSample>.

=head1 JSON AND COMMAND-LINE USE

=item Add separate version-controlled JSON example files for each principal
layout.

=item Add more tests that exercise the installed C<font-sample> command.

=item Add tests that explicitly verify multi-page comparison and character
output.

=item Review command-line diagnostics and error messages for missing fonts,
bad paths, unsupported layouts, and malformed configuration files.

=head1 FONT PROVIDERS

=item Keep C<App::FontSample> provider-neutral. Font discovery, installation,
and collection-specific behavior should remain outside the core sampler.

=item Continue testing C<NotoFonts-OT> as an optional integration rather than
making it a required dependency.

=item Consider a separate helper or system tool for discovering and
installing additional Noto fonts and font weights.

=head1 API AND INTERNAL CLEANUP

=item Review whether C<App::FontSample::Provider> is still useful. Remove it
in a later API cleanup if the C<PDF::Content::FontObj> interface has made it
obsolete.

=item Review public option names as the layouts mature and keep common
options consistent across layouts.

=item Continue separating font acquisition, page description, and layout
rendering so new layouts do not require changes to font-provider code.

=head1 DOCUMENTATION

=item Add visual PDF examples to the published documentation when there is a
practical way to distribute and maintain them.

=item Keep optional native-library requirements with the documentation for
the font loader or provider that requires them rather than presenting them as
requirements of the provider-neutral core.

=end pod
